  "id": "BIT-phpmyadmin-2026-119563",
  "summary": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 Stored XSS via Designer Query History Table Name",
  "details": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows database users with CREATE privilege to inject script via unescaped table names in DesignerHistory.display(). Attackers can create a table whose name contains HTML markup that executes in another user's session when they add a condition on it in Designer query mode.",
